<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Russo-Persian War (1826–1828)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1826–1828</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Russo-Persian War of 1826–1828 began when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, led by Crown Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbas-mirza">Abbas Mirza</a>, attacked Russian-held territory in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-caucasus">South Caucasus</a> to recover lands lost in 1813. After early successes the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a> were defeated at Ganja, and the Russians under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-paskevich">Ivan Paskevich</a> took Erivan and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-turkmenchay">Treaty of Turkmenchay</a> of 1828 ceded the khanates of Erivan and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nakhchivan">Nakhichevan</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and made the Aras river the border.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/russo-persian-war-1826-1828.jpg" alt="Russo-Persian War (1826–1828)" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Литография Г. Беггрова по оригиналу В. Машкова · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_near_Elisavetpol.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
